      "If you study in a group, do not use the group to share memorised answers. Use it to mark each other against the command word. Read a question aloud, hear three attempts, and decide which one actually did the verb. That is a legitimate use of past papers: they supply the verbs and the topics. Your group supplies the honesty.",
      "The last week before the exam is late to sit a paper you then refuse to mark. It is not late to sit one section, mark it the same evening, and repair one cluster. Diagnosis can be small. What does not help is rereading old solutions until they feel familiar and calling that familiarity readiness.",
