      "When a calculation goes wrong, do not scribble it out into a black cloud. Put one line through the error and continue underneath. Markers will follow the surviving path. If you change a reading, change it in the table as well so the working still matches the data. Inconsistency between table and calculation is a way to lose both the data mark and the method mark.",
